      en: "The Vallée des Couleurs Nature Park in southern Mauritius is a unique geological and leisure center. Its main attraction is the 23-colored earth, the result of various oxides and minerals formed during volcanic activity. This colorful hillside creates a spectacular contrast with the surrounding green forests. However, the park is not only a feast for the eyes but also awaits adrenaline lovers: it is home to the longest zipline in the Indian Ocean, as well as quad bike tours, suspension bridges, and a series of waterfalls. Several native animal species, including tortoises and deer, can be observed in the park. Vallée des Couleurs is the perfect meeting of the power of nature and modern adventure tourism. Geography K5 — Volcanic Activity and Rocks."
